# Copy this to mcpo.env BEFORE the first `docker compose up` (mcpo's compose entry references
# ./mcpo-secrets/mcpo.env as a second env_file -- a missing file makes `docker compose up` fail
# to start ANY service, same as mcpo/config.json.example's existing requirement).
#
# You do not need to edit this file directly. Once the stack is running, set these values from
# the dashboard: SETTINGS (gear icon) -> SECRETS -> "Portfolio (Monarch)" / "Market data" groups.
# portfolio-api OVERWRITES this file's contents whenever you save there -- manual edits here will
# be replaced. It starts empty; leaving it empty is fine (Monarch/Tavily just stay unconfigured
# until you fill them in, exactly like leaving the fields blank in .env used to work).
#
# Run `docker compose up -d mcpo` after saving a change here for it to take effect -- NOT
# `docker compose restart mcpo`, which reuses the container's existing environment and will not
# pick up an edited env_file. Same "recreate to apply" story as portfolio-api's own settings.
